speechtext:
Paragraph (q) of section 14 says:
[DOT]-and in particular to guarantee the payment of dividends, or the payment of the principal of and interest on debentures or other securities, mortgages and liabilities of any such company;
It seems to me that a great deal of fraud might creep into the handling of a company where one company is permitted to guarantee the dividends of another. I can understand that an occasion might arise when it might be necessary and advisable to do that, but in my opinion it should be done only upon application to the department of the Secretary of State, or something of the kind, rather than that the company should be granted this power upon incorporation.
